# Content conventions

Details: `docs/design/content.md`.

## Article files
An article is one file in `src/content/articles/en/<slug>.md` or `src/content/articles/my/<slug>.md`. A matching file in the other folder is optional; the same file name links the language switcher. Slugs are English Latin letters. See `.cursor/rules/i18n.mdc`.

## Article frontmatter
Validated by `src/content.config.ts`; the build fails on invalid data. Keep the same fields in `public/admin/config.yml`. `title` and `description` are in the article's own language.
```yaml
---
title: 'Hip replacement abroad: costs, recovery, and risks' # quote titles containing a colon
description: One or two plain-language sentences for listings and search results.
pubDate: 2026-11-12
updatedDate: 2026-12-01 # set when content is materially revised
draft: false
---
```
Adding or renaming a frontmatter field is top-layer: update the schema, `docs/design/content.md`, and the changelog.

## Article body
- Never use `#` in the body; the title renders as the `h1`. Use `##` for sections, `###` for subsections, in order.
- Open with a short summary answering the main question.
- Short paragraphs; lists for steps, symptoms, options.
- End clinical content with `## Sources` (primary sources) and a note that it is general information, not medical advice.
- No inline HTML classes or styles in Markdown. New elements go in `.prose-content` or an MDX component.

## Voice
Plain language, "you", outcome first, explain terms on first use. No superlatives without evidence, no promised outcomes. Same rules in Myanmar.

## Trust details on pages
- Show published and updated dates.
- Prices: range, currency, date checked, inclusions and exclusions.
- Accreditation: name the body and link to verification.
- Inquiry points: a short numbered "what happens next" list.

## Pages
- Every page uses `MainLayout` with `title` and `description`, taken from `src/i18n/ui.ts` or the article.
- Page markup lives in a view in `src/views/`, rendered by an English route and a Myanmar route under `src/pages/my/`.
- Treatment guides follow the section order in `docs/design/content.md`.
- LINE, Viber, Messenger, and Facebook details live only in `contactChannels` in `src/lib/site.ts` (used by the contact page and footer). Do not hard-code numbers or profile URLs in views or components. No phone row on the contact page.
- Viber numbers are chosen from a native `<details>` list (`ViberNumbers`), never a modal. Links with an `appHref` render `data-app-href` and rely on `src/scripts/app-links.ts`.
